  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-07-18T14:04:28.676Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It was only a matter of time until an exploit would break every Udon-based user authentication system over night, but here we are.\nAffected is:\n- every Udon moderation tool\n- every Udon whitelisting tool\n- every Patreon enhancement system\n- every access control system for private worlds that should stay private until they are released, but need to have public test user sessions\nThe situation right now: People go in worlds, gain access that they should not have, and ruin other people's fun by pretending to be the world author.\nHere is my proposed solution which would allow us to \"fix\" this:\n1. Private user certificates\n- every user needs a private certificate in their client, which can be used to encrypt or sign a synced string in a function like EncryptString(string input) which returns the string encrypted with that local private certificate.\n2. Public user certificates\n- every user needs access to the public certificates of other users to be able to decript a string in a function like DecryptString(string encryptedStr, string userID)\n- the userID needs to be the one from the VRChat website, or alternatively the display name (please don't), only having the public certificate from others in your current instance would not be enough\nThe goal of this is to allow a safe user-to-user communication in which you can trust that whatever arrives on your side from the network to really be from that specific user, and that a user who pretends to be user X is able to decrypt a secret string which was encrypted by that user's certificate once. On top of that, authenticating a network-event (knowing where it came from) would also allow additional security.",
